    {
      "id": "medina-blake",
      "nationId": "spanish",
      "name": "Blake's Army of Galicia",
      "formation": "Vanguard, 1st and 4th Divisions",
      "side": "Spanish",
      "summary": "Blake's regulars and militia held the low ridge in front of Medina. Merle's attack turned their left on the Monclin heights; Blake's counter-attack was beaten off, and when the French drove between his army and Cuesta's the Galicians broke, losing their guns.",
      "notes": [
        "After Nafziger. Each division is shown as one brigade; the half-battalions of volunteers are Small light battalions.",
        "The 1st Division's Militia Grenadiers were two battalions; one is shown. More Militia and Line regiments in a brigade than the list allows show as historical departures.",
        "The Spanish cavalry regiments were mere squadrons, a hundred or so men, so they are Small; a cavalry brigade of them, short of the heavy regiments it needs, shows as a historical departure.",
        "Three batteries of five or six guns for twenty-odd battalions show as a historical departure.",
        "Commanders are at Staff Rating 8, the default for historical forces; but Brig Conde de Maceda at 7, the most the list allows; Mariscal de Campo Cagigal at 7, the most the list allows; Mariscal de Campo Marqués de Portago at 7, the most the list allows; Vanguard Cavalry at 7, the most the list allows."
